{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI reached Amsterdam shortly after noon, my legs still aching from the journey. I went straight to Dr. Besseling, who received me with the courtesy Mr. van Ghert promised. We spoke little of philosophy, mostly of the weather, which here is as grey as a Nuremberg winter.\n\nThen I visited the picture gallery. The scale of it is staggering; the Rembrandts are vast, fifteen to twenty feet across. Standing before them, one feels the weight of history pressing in. I confess I could not view the whole collection today; the mind requires rest as much as the body.\n\nI hope the boys are well and that you are not too tired. I think of our quiet evenings in Berlin, and how the noise of travel makes one appreciate the silence of home. I will send word when I leave.\n\nYour devoted,\nG.W.F."}}],"created":1795080115,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":187,"prompt_tokens":938,"total_tokens":1125,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-zfQuyHbqJgfCLynTXmqlhcBYWRBKaOAG","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":938,"prompt_ms":914.549,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9749989339019189,"prompt_per_second":1025.6421471129486,"predicted_n":187,"predicted_ms":4385.906,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.580139784946237,"predicted_per_second":42.4085696319073}}